    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        1320,
        900
      ],
      "size": [
        820,
        330
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 1,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "How this works",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "1. Upload your video (Source video; trim it with Trim Video if needed) and a clear photo of the product (Product photo).\n2. Split Video by Scene cuts it into scenes. The contact sheet shows them numbered from 0.\n3. Gemini runs once per scene and answers whether the product is in it (JSON).\n4. Scene Gate passes only the product scenes on. With none, nothing after it runs.\n5. Pad Video brings short scenes up to the video model's minimum by repeating the last frame\n   (Seedance 2.5 edit needs 4-30 s; set 0 for a model with no minimum).\n6. The video model runs once per product scene, all at the same time. The switch picks it:\n   off = Seedance 2.5 edit (padded to 4 s), on = Wan 3.0 Reference to Video (no minimum,\n   max 15 s per scene; its duration is set per scene by Video Duration). Only the picked\n   model runs. Raw outputs are saved too.\n7. Join Scenes puts each swap back in its slot, keeps exactly the original frames\n   (padding dropped), resizes to the source and plays the source audio under everything.\n\nLook at one scene: un-bypass 'Look at one scene' + 'Picked scene' (Ctrl+B) and set the index.\nCosts: Gemini once per scene, Seedance once per product scene. Seeds are fixed, so\nre-queuing with nothing changed reuses the cached results."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "1. Upload your video (Source video; trim it with Trim Video if needed) and a clear photo of the product (Product photo).\n2. Split Video by Scene cuts it into scenes. The contact sheet shows them numbered from 0.\n3. Gemini runs once per scene and answers whether the product is in it (JSON).\n4. Scene Gate passes only the product scenes on. With none, nothing after it runs.\n5. Pad Video brings short scenes up to the video model's minimum by repeating the last frame\n   (Seedance 2.5 edit needs 4-30 s; set 0 for a model with no minimum).\n6. The video model runs once per product scene, all at the same time. The switch picks it:\n   off = Seedance 2.5 edit (padded to 4 s), on = Wan 3.0 Reference to Video (no minimum,\n   max 15 s per scene; its duration is set per scene by Video Duration). Only the picked\n   model runs. Raw outputs are saved too.\n7. Join Scenes puts each swap back in its slot, keeps exactly the original frames\n   (padding dropped), resizes to the source and plays the source audio under everything.\n\nLook at one scene: un-bypass 'Look at one scene' + 'Picked scene' (Ctrl+B) and set the index.\nCosts: Gemini once per scene, Seedance once per product scene. Seeds are fixed, so\nre-queuing with nothing changed reuses the cached results."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
